{"text": "5898 Peterson Ridge Lane Memphis, TN 38135\n901-305-7129 keithsandersgroup@gmail.com\n\nKEITH SANDERS\n\nDetermined professional with a proven success in school turnaround, educational process optimization, team\nmentorship, and instruction improvement, as well as exceptional communication and leadership acumen seeking a\nchallenging position to contribute to the educational success through exceptional ability to collaborate with diverse\n\ngroups, perform effective decision-making, and sustain superior motivation to attain established objectives\n\nSUMMARY OF QUALIFICATIONS\n\nRelationship-Builder | Problem-Solver | Team-Player | Analytical Thinker | Self-Directed | Highly-Organized | Detail-Oriented\nData Analysis | Employee mentorship | Staff Development | Curriculum/Instructional Supervision | Program Evaluation | Parental\nInvolvement Workshops | Learning & Teaching Assessments | Graduation & Acceptance Rate Optimization\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\nKEITH SANDERS GROUP, INC.\nChief Executive Officer 2014-present\ne Execute the overall mission of the organization and evaluate performance\ne Support district leaders and teachers in implementing curriculum\ne Oversee expansion and new projects\ne Design professional development\n\nThe John Maxwell Team\nJohn Maxwell Certified Coach, Teacher and Speaker 2013-present\ne Leadership Development\ne Professional Coaching\ne Professional Speaking\nDELAWARE DEPARTMENT OF EDUCATION\nChief Officer of School Turnaround 2012-2014\ne Supported the Implementation of School Success Plans for bottom 5% of schools in Delaware. As a result, 9 of the 23\npriority/focus schools ranked in the top 35 of all schools in the state based on one years growth measures in ELA and Math. 3\nschools ranked in the top 5 and 4 in the top 10.\ne Developed Education Policy to Support Implementation\ne Managed Race to the Top Funds for the persistently low achieving schools named to the Partnership Zone as well as all\nidentified focus schools\nMILLER McCoy NETWORK\nCo-Chief Executive Officer 2010-2012\ne\u00a2 Co-Founded Miller McCoy Academy Denver (scheduled opening: fall 2013)\ne Conceptualized and resourcefully integrated comprehensive educational activities to provide a value-added and efficient\nlearning experience, resulting in students success enhancement and continuous learning progress sustainment\ne Ensure superior compliance with State Department Of Education regulations, as well as conduct masterful research to\nefficiently evaluate latest educational trends/needs, consequently establishing and adjusting program directions accordingly\nMILLER MCCoy ACADEMY FOR MATHEMATICS AND BUSINESS\nCo-Founder and High School Principal 2007-2012\ne Introduced and successfully maintain a culture of data-driven instruction, while resourcefully implementing Professional\nLearning Communities; set and proactively communicate program priorities to ensure consistent compliance and attainment\ne Secured and masterfully develop collaborative partnerships with key Community Stakeholders\ne Developed Effective Professional Development program to optimize the Social Studies and Language Arts areas\n\ne Implemented positive behavior and compelling attendance initiatives, resulting in students success improvement",
